# ── Deployment secrets ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The hosted database's connection string and the API's signing key. These are
# live credentials for a publicly reachable deployment: a leaked connection
# string is direct database access, and a leaked signing key lets anyone mint a
# token for any member.
#
# Kept in a file rather than in shell history so they are not re-typed, and
# ignored so they cannot be committed by accident.
.env.deploy
.env.deploy.*

# ── Documentation is not committed ───────────────────────────────────────────
# Reports, matrices, reviews and phase write-ups stay local.
*.md
docs/

# -- ...but two of those are build inputs, not documentation ------------------
#
# Roslyn analyzer release tracking is .md by convention, and
# Diaspora.Analyzers.csproj lists both files as compile inputs. The blanket
# rule above caught them by extension.
#
# They exist in every working tree, so nothing local ever fails. The only
# place it appears is a clean checkout -- CI, a new machine, a release build:
#
#     CSC : error CS2001: Source file AnalyzerReleases.Shipped.md
#           could not be found.
#
# Recorded as UAT-131. Re-inclusion works because the exclusion is on the
# extension, not on a parent directory; git cannot re-include a file whose
# directory is itself excluded, which is why docs/ needs different treatment
# and has not been given one here.
!src/Diaspora.Analyzers/AnalyzerReleases.Shipped.md
!src/Diaspora.Analyzers/AnalyzerReleases.Unshipped.md
.neon
.env.local
node_modules/
